{"file": "C:/Users/Garrett/Sports/docs/arxiv-program/research/2026-09-21/arxiv-program/index/IMPROVEMENT-LEDGER.md", "equation": "Change:** Build a season-episode trajectory dataset for staking: one 'episode' = one NFL season of weekly slates; per week t: R-hat_t = remaining season profit target in units, s_t = slate features (edges, CLV, bankroll, week number, exposure used), a_t = stake-bucket vector (discrete 0/0.25/0.5/1/2u per bet, padded); train a small GPT (4-6 layers, 18-week or K=8 context) with CE loss on stake tokens conditioned on R-hat_1 = +30u season target; each Tuesday prompt with the remaining target and recent (R-hat, s, a) history to emit the week's stake vector — then extend to distributional conditioning: quantile targets (e.g., 'achieve >=+20u with P(drawdown>10u) <= 0.1') as additional conditioning tokens with a quantile-weighted loss.", "page_or_eqnum": null, "wave": 9140}
